<%# Shared controls for a feature page's header: on/off, plus (Admin-only) Solo Admin,
    Modificabile, and Riordina card — rendered as one connected segmented button group,
    active state colored (accent), inactive using the default muted button color. Started
    as an experiment on Anime Night only (partials/featureToggleGrouped.ejs); once the user
    liked it, it became the standard here so every current AND future feature page gets it
    automatically just by including this partial, same as before.
    Each item is still a real (hidden) checkbox under the hood — only the visual skin is a
    button group instead of individual switches (public/style.css's .btn-group rules).
    Active/colored state is driven purely by CSS `:has(input:checked)` (same technique
    already used in channelpermissions.ejs), no JS or server-computed class needed.
    Wrapped in one outer div so `.page-header`'s flex layout (h1 vs. everything else) still
    only ever sees two children, regardless of how many buttons actually render.
    Locals: `enabled` (bool), `toggleAction` (the feature's own POST /<feature>/toggle
    route — already expects `enabled` as the literal string "true"/"false"). A single
    checkbox works here without a hidden fallback field: every route already reads
    `req.body.enabled === 'true'`, and an unchecked checkbox simply omits `enabled` from
    the POST body entirely, which that comparison already treats as false. %>
<div class="feature-toggle-group">
  <div class="btn-group">
    <form method="POST" action="<%= toggleAction %>" class="btn-group-form">
      <label class="btn-group-item">
        <input type="checkbox" name="enabled" value="true" <%= enabled ? 'checked' : '' %> onchange="this.form.submit()" />
        <span>Active</span>
      </label>
    </form>

    <%# Admin-only: whether this feature's page is also opened to the server's Mod role.
        Set globally by requireDashboardAccess (middleware/requireAdmin.js), not passed by
        each route — `role`/`currentFeatureKey`/`modAccessEnabled` are all res.locals
        already. Mods themselves never see this (their `role` is 'mod'), so they can't
        grant themselves more access. Toggling it doesn't affect what a Mod can do INSIDE
        an already-allowed feature — that's always full parity with Admin — only whether
        they can open this page at all. Label is always "Solo Admin" — colored (active)
        means mods are locked out, uncolored means they're allowed; the checkbox name
        `soloAdmin` is intentionally the inverse of `modAccessEnabled`, so the route
        computes `allowed = req.body.soloAdmin !== 'true'` (unchecked → allowed). %>
    <% if (typeof role !== 'undefined' && role === 'admin' && typeof currentFeatureKey !== 'undefined' && currentFeatureKey) { %>
      <form method="POST" action="/mod-access/<%= currentFeatureKey %>/toggle" class="btn-group-form">
        <label class="btn-group-item">
          <input type="checkbox" name="soloAdmin" value="true" <%= modAccessEnabled ? '' : 'checked' %> onchange="this.form.submit()" />
          <span>Admin only</span>
        </label>
      </form>
    <% } %>

    <%# Admin-only TO CHANGE: freezes this feature's own add/edit/remove/reorder forms (its
        list of items) without touching the on/off toggle above or base config (channel/
        role/schedule) — the feature keeps doing whatever it already does (e.g. QOTD keeps
        posting on schedule) while locked, only the dashboard's own CRUD forms are blocked
        (enforced centrally in requireDashboardAccess, for Admin and Mod alike). Posts to a
        route generic across every feature page — `featureLocked` local set by the same
        middleware, and Admin-only server-side too (routes/featureLockRoutes.js 403s a Mod
        POST), so a Mod gets a disabled, read-only copy of the same button below instead of
        this interactive one — just enough to see whether the feature is currently locked
        (and why their own add/edit/remove forms might be blocked), not to change it. Label
        is always "Edit" — colored (active) means editable, uncolored means locked; the
        checkbox name `editable` is intentionally the inverse of `featureLocked`, so the
        route computes `locked = req.body.editable !== 'true'` (unchecked → locked). %>
    <% if (typeof role !== 'undefined' && role === 'admin' && typeof currentFeatureKey !== 'undefined' && currentFeatureKey) { %>
      <form method="POST" action="/feature-lock/<%= currentFeatureKey %>/toggle" class="btn-group-form">
        <label class="btn-group-item">
          <input type="checkbox" name="editable" value="true" <%= typeof featureLocked !== 'undefined' && featureLocked ? '' : 'checked' %> onchange="this.form.submit()" />
          <span>Edit</span>
        </label>
      </form>
    <% } else if (typeof role !== 'undefined' && role === 'mod' && typeof featureLocked !== 'undefined') { %>
      <label class="btn-group-item btn-group-item-readonly" title="Solo un Admin può cambiarlo">
        <input type="checkbox" <%= featureLocked ? '' : 'checked' %> disabled />
        <span>Edit</span>
      </label>
    <% } %>

    <%# Card-reorder + card-resize support: `cardOrder` (drag order) and `cardSizes` (grid
        column/row span) are always set by requireDashboardAccess, for both Admin and Mod,
        so both apply for anyone viewing the page — only this button + the drag handles/
        resize grips it reveals are Admin-only. See public/cardReorder.js and each view's
        `<div class="card-list" id="card-list">` wrapping its `.panel[data-card-id]`
        sections — the standard for every feature page, current and future. Unlike the
        three items above, this one is NOT wired to submit-on-change: it's a pure
        client-side mode toggle (unlocked = draggable + resizable) handled entirely by
        cardReorder.js, which decides on its own whether re-locking needs to POST the
        hidden #card-reorder-form below (only if something was actually dragged or resized
        — see that file). Label is always "Riordina card". %>
    <% if (typeof cardOrder !== 'undefined') { %>
      <script id="card-order-data" type="application/json"><%- JSON.stringify(cardOrder) %></script>
    <% } %>
    <%# Saved per-card CSS Grid span, keyed by data-card-id — an empty object on a page
        nobody has resized yet, harmless (every card just keeps its default full-width
        span). Applied on load and re-saved alongside order in the same
        #card-reorder-form/POST — see cardReorder.js and the "sizes" field handling in
        routes/cardOrderRoutes.js. %>
    <% if (typeof cardSizes !== 'undefined') { %>
      <script id="card-size-data" type="application/json"><%- JSON.stringify(cardSizes) %></script>
    <% } %>
    <% if (typeof role !== 'undefined' && role === 'admin' && typeof currentFeatureKey !== 'undefined' && currentFeatureKey) { %>
      <label class="btn-group-item">
        <input type="checkbox" id="card-lock-btn" />
        <span>Reorder</span>
      </label>
      <form id="card-reorder-form" method="POST" action="/card-order/<%= currentFeatureKey %>/reorder" style="display:none;">
        <input type="hidden" id="card-order-input" name="order" value="" />
        <input type="hidden" id="card-size-input" name="sizes" value="" />
      </form>
    <% } %>
  </div>
</div>
<script src="/cardReorder.js"></script>
